# Review: plugin-crm

The deterministic core is solid and tested. `ProcessMailbox` sends each sender through
`@dxos/extractor-lib`'s `buildContactFromActor`, using the space's identity index. It records
provenance with `Mailbox.recordExtraction` and advances a tagged feed `Cursor`.
`ResearchPerson` and `ResearchOrganization` render the section template, parent the document to the
subject and upsert a `ProfileOf` relation. `process-mailbox.test.ts` and `research.test.ts` cover
T-1 to T-3 end to end. The CRM nav group and its type nodes exist and open plugin-space's
`TypeArticle`.

The agentic half is thin. The skill instructions do not describe the Person, Organization and
Message branches (F-1.2, F-1.3). They do not mention free-mail domains (F-3.5) or list registered
research sources (F-7.3). The skill declares no dependency on the web-search, database or markdown
skills. The skill tests are `it.effect.skip` with no assertions, so T-4 to T-6 have no automation.
The biggest divergence is `attachImage`. It reads the image service URL from an input override or
`DX_CRM_IMAGE_SERVICE_URL`, not from `@dxos/config`, so an agent call without the override fails. Every
failure is one `AttachImageError`, not a `ConfigMissing`, `FetchFailed` or other tagged error, and no
test runs the operation. `ContactExtract` does not exist; extraction moved to extractor-lib.

## Extensions

| Term      | URI                        |
| --------- | -------------------------- |
| `verdict` | `org.dxos.mdl.verdict@1.0` |

